OL,3,GNEWSASafety advice ahead of flaming tar
OL,4,Abarrel event
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople planning to attend a town where
OL,7,Fflaming tar barrels are carried along
OL,8,Fthe streets for Bonfire Night have been
OL,9,Fasked not to "abandon" their cars for
OL,10,Fsafety reasons.
OL,12,FThe Ottery St Mary Tar Barrels, held
OL,13,Fannually on 5 November, involves people
OL,14,Fknown as "barrel rollers" running
OL,15,Fthrough the Devon town with 27 flaming
OL,16,Ftar-soaked barrels while thousands of
OL,17,Fspectators line the streets.
OL,19,FOrganisers said: "Abandoning your car
OL,20,Fon the event clearways and emergency
OL,21,Fevacuation routes is not acceptable and
OL,22,Fjeopardises the safety of the event."
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
